---
/**
 * THE BOLT — /privacy. Carried over from the Next site's policy (July 11, 2026) and corrected
 * for how THIS site handles data. Keep it true: if a data flow changes, change this page and
 * UPDATED in the same commit.
 *
 * What changed from the Next policy, and why:
 *   - SongRank taps are stored (D1 `ranks`: track, rating, time, hashed IP) and summarised in
 *     an hourly email, instead of one email per vote; they aren't Turnstile-checked.
 *   - Local storage now holds the theme choice, the listener's own ratings and player volume
 *     (the Next site kept a stream-quality choice).
 *   - No analytics: this site doesn't load Cloudflare Web Analytics.
 *   - Stored editorial content is the airplay chart and the play log (no schedule).
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteMast from '../components/SiteMast.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import ContactDialog from '../components/ContactDialog.astro';
import { station } from '../config/station';

const UPDATED = 'November 9, 2026';
const PRIVACY_EMAIL = 'info@clubfm.stream';
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${station.name}`}
  description={`How ${station.name} handles your data: what we keep when you listen, rate a song, request one, or get in touch, and what we never do with it.`}
>
  <div class="site">
    <SiteMast />

    <main class="log page wrap">
      <a class="log__back t-mono" href="/">← Back to on air</a>

      <div class="log__intro">
        <h1 class="log__h t-display">Privacy</h1>
        <p class="prose__date t-mono">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2 class="t-display">The short version</h2>
        <p>
          The BOLT is a free radio stream. There are no accounts, no ads, no tracking cookies and no
          analytics, and we never sell data. The only personal details we receive are the ones you
          type into the contact form, and we use them only to reply.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-display">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          The BOLT ({station.domain}) is a station of the ClubFM network, operated by Radiant Ventures.
          For anything privacy-related, email <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-display">Listening</h2>
        <p>
          Listening needs no account and no personal details. Like any web server, our streaming
          servers log standard connection data (IP address, user agent) for operations, capacity
          planning and aggregate listener counts. We don’t use those logs to identify or profile
          listeners.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-display">SongRank ratings</h2>
        <p>
          When you rate a song we store the track, your rating, the time, and a hashed form of your
          IP address (never the address itself). The hash lets us limit repeat votes; we don’t use it
          to identify you. Ratings are summarised in an hourly email to the station. Your own ratings
          are also kept in your browser so the site can show them back to you.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-display">Song requests and the contact form</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>A song request</strong> contains only the song and artist you type. It reaches us as
          an email.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The contact form</strong> asks for your name, email address, an optional company or
          artist name, and your message. We use them only to read and answer you. They’re delivered to
          our mailboxes and kept only as long as the conversation needs.
        </p>
        <p>
          Both are sent by <a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resend</a>,
          our email provider, to mailboxes hosted by Spacemail. When you submit, your IP address is
          used briefly for rate limiting and bot protection; it isn’t included in the email we receive
          for a request.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-display">Bot protection</h2>
        <p>
          Requests and the contact form are protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, an invisible check with
          no puzzles or checkboxes. To tell people from bots, Turnstile processes a limited set of
          signals: your IP address, TLS fingerprint, user agent, and the site key and origin.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cloudflare says these signals are used only to detect and block bots, not to identify,
          profile or target anyone, and it processes them for us and to improve its own bot
          detection. See the
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Turnstile Privacy Policy</a>
          and the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-display">Hosting and security</h2>
        <p>
          The site runs on Cloudflare Workers. Cloudflare processes connection data, including IP
          addresses, to deliver the site and to protect it (DDoS protection, firewall, rate limiting).
          The content we keep there, the airplay chart and the play log, is about the music, not about
          visitors.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-display">Cookies and local storage</h2>
        <p>
          We set no advertising or tracking cookies, and we run no analytics. Your browser’s local
          storage keeps a few things that never leave your device:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>your light/dark choice, which lapses after a week away;</li>
          <li>the ratings you’ve given, so the site can show them back to you;</li>
          <li>the player’s volume.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          A session cookie is set only on the staff admin pages, only for staff who sign in there.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-display">What we never do</h2>
        <p>
          We don’t sell or rent data, run advertising or ad tech, build listener profiles, or share
          personal information beyond the providers named above (Cloudflare, Resend, Spacemail), each
          of which handles it only to provide its service to us.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-display">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may have the right to see, correct or delete personal data
          we hold, which for this site mostly means contact-form correspondence. Email
          <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a> and we’ll handle it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-display">Children</h2>
        <p>
          The BOLT is a general-audience stream with no accounts, and doesn’t knowingly collect
          personal information from children.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-display">Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If our practices change, we’ll update this page and the date at the top.
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>

    <SiteFooter />
  </div>

  <ContactDialog />

  <script>
    import '../scripts/contact.ts';
  </script>
</Base>
